<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Synthetic Lanelet2 fixture: a junction whose connecting lanes fan out to
  two different outgoing roads.

  Layout (looking from above, driving direction +x, lanes about 3.5 m wide):
    incoming road  A1/A2/A3 (ids 5001-5003)   local_x 81700 -> 81720
    junction       J1/J2/J3 (ids 5004-5006)   local_x 81720 -> 81735, turn_direction=straight
    outgoing       X  (id 5007, one lane, straight on)   local_x 81735 -> 81755
                   Y1/Y2 (ids 5008-5009, two lanes, bending right)
  J1 continues into X; J2 and J3 continue into Y1 and Y2.  X and Y share
  the node where J1 and J2 meet but no boundary way, so they become two
  separate OpenDRIVE roads; J1-J3 are laterally adjacent and become a
  one-lane connecting road (J1) and a two-lane one (J2, J3).

  The connecting road can carry a single road-level <successor> (X); the
  lanes continuing into Y must not emit <successor id> values that only
  exist in Y, because CARLA reads them against X.

  Node lat/lon place the layout (local_x -> east, local_y -> north); the
  local_x/local_y tags follow the other mini fixtures and are not read.
-->
<osm generator="junction_fanout_mini_fixture">
